    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "L3 exposure records provide Cmax/AUC but not F values, so they cannot resolve the F ≥ 20% threshold directly.",
    "The query's D-ring modification (tertiary C17 hydroxyl plus extra ring) is not represented in any L1/L2/L3 record with a measured absolute bioavailability.",
    "Transfer from estradiol (low F) versus ethinyl estradiol (higher F) is ambiguous because the query lacks the ethynyl group but retains a tertiary C17 hydroxyl."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L3 oral exposure records are contextually relevant but do not provide affirmative F evidence; estradiol exposure is low, while ethinyl estradiol exposure is higher but the query lacks the ethynyl group. The prior low prediction from L1/L2 steroid contexts remains supported, so the decision is kept as low with high confidence."
}

